        {
          "path": "_m/w/2/1/z/civilian-war-memorial-wp/memorial-civilian-vict.jpg",
          "filename": "Memorial to the Civilian Victims of the Japanese Occupation.jpg",
          "caption": "The Memorial to the Civilian Victims of the Japanese Occupation is a war memorial in Singapore built in memory of the civilians killed during the Japanese occupation of Singapore during World War II. It is located in Singapore's Central Area near City Hall and the central business district. It was officially unveiled by then Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew on February 15, 1967, which was the 25th anniversary of the fall of Singapore, and gazetted as a national memorial on August 15, 2013. The imposing structure comprises four tapering columns with an approximate height of 68 meters. The columns represent the merging of four streams of culture into one and the principle of unity of all races. Usually taken from the side, the picture shows a unique angle, taken from the centre of the memorial upwards, resulting in a cross-like shape.",
          "alt": "The Memorial to the Civilian Victims of the Japanese Occupation is a war memorial in Singapore built in memory of the civilians killed during the Japanese occupation of Singapore during World War II. It is located in Singapore's Central Area near City Hall and the central business district. It was officially unveiled by then Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew on February 15, 1967, which was the 25th anniversary of the fall of Singapore, and gazetted as a national memorial on August 15, 2013. The imposing structure comprises four tapering columns with an approximate height of 68 meters. The columns represent the merging of four streams of culture into one and the principle of unity of all races. Usually taken from the side, the picture shows a unique angle, taken from the centre of the memorial upwards, resulting in a cross-like shape.",
          "width": 4316,
          "height": 2859,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "MikedSG2001",
